 {"id":"CF-376","title":"The worker seat names a pair the router registry does not carry: worker_model deepseek-v4-flash@deepseek-foreman is absent from the registry CF-245 validates pins against","status":"pending","priority":"P2","complexity":2,"created_at":"2026-11-06T06:03:32Z","updated_at":"2026-11-06T06:03:32Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"815ad62de001b1218e9148b4dbae5b909b4c65df94fdf22ae715a5ad5e7f71e4"},"reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-06 by tick code-factory-2026-11-06-04-01-25, while closing CF-245.\n\nCF-245's guard (scheduler repo commit 572b111f: internal/config/pin_registry.go + pin_registry_test.go + loader.go wiring, 4 tests PASS on origin/main e46f2252) validates the LANE pin: the (model, provider) pair in fleet.toml's [[projects]] block. The WORKER seat of the same lane is not covered, and it currently names a pair the registry does not carry.\n\nEvidence, all re-runnable:\n  sqlite3 ~/.hermes/scheduler.db \"select name,model,provider,worker_model,worker_provider from projects where name='code-factory';\"\n    code-factory|deepseek-flash|deepseek-foreman|deepseek-v4-flash|deepseek-foreman\n  python3 - <<'PY' over task-router/registry.json (tables.models)\n    deepseek-foreman rows: deepseek-flash (enabled), deepseek-v4-pro (enabled), deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp (enabled but valid_to 2026-09-10)\n    deepseek-v4-flash rows: clinepass (enabled), commandcode (enabled) - never deepseek-foreman\n\nSo the tick seat (model/provider) is a registry pair that CF-245's validator would pass, while the worker seat (worker_model/worker_provider) is the NOT-IN-REGISTRY shape the same validator was built to name. The dispatch still worked: this tick's worker ran on deepseek-v4-flash@deepseek-foreman and committed (2ef9cfe, later discarded as a duplicate - see the CF-245 event), so the provider accepts the name as an alias while the registry - the artifact the pin validator and the scheduler's rating logic read - does not know it. Every worker dispatch on this lane therefore has a model_served that cannot be attributed from the registry, which is exactly the unmeasured-pin class CF-245 closed, one layer down.","acceptance_criteria":"1. One command re-measures the class fleet-wide: for every projects row carrying a non-empty worker_model AND worker_provider, resolve the pair against registry tables.models and print the count of rows naming an absent or disabled pair plus the names. Before the fix it names code-factory (and any sibling lane with the same drift); after the fix it prints 0.\n2. Either the worker seats are corrected to registry pairs in both stores that outrank the router (scheduler.db projects.worker_model/worker_provider and fleet.toml if the lane carries the mirror), or the registry gains an entry for the alias that states what actually serves it. The row records which shape was chosen, the file, and the exact edit - no silent third option.\n3. The guard covers the worker seat, not only the lane pin: a fixture project naming an absent or disabled worker pair produces the named warning, proven by a test in the scheduler repo that goes red when the worker-seat coverage is removed (the same red/green discipline pin_registry_test.go uses for the lane pin).\n4. The row states whether any worker dispatch produced an unattributable model_served: read state.db session_model_usage for this lane's worker sessions and report the served model, rather than asserting the seat from its label.","probe":null,"capability_tags":["config-validation","registry","worker-seat"]}
